# ====================
# Node.js
# ====================
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
# package-lock.json is COMMITTED on purpose. It used to be ignored here,
# inherited from a generic Node template, and the cost was invisible: with
# no lockfile in the repository `npm ci` could not run at all, so CI
# installed with `npm install` and re-resolved every caret range on every
# run. The release then compiled a dependency set nobody had tested. The
# test workflow, which does call `npm ci`, had been failing on every push
# for the same reason. mopro_bindings has its own entry further down.

# ====================
# Yarn
# ====================
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions

